
--- Conflict encountered: cherry-pick reported a modify/delete conflict ---
Why: cherry-pick 3-way-merges against the PARENT of the picked commit as the
base. That base (still on feature-branch) already has feature.txt, but main
never had feature.txt at all (main never merged the earlier feature commits
that created it) - so relative to that base, main looks like it "deleted" the
file. Git flags this as a modify/delete conflict even though really this is
just a new file being introduced.

Resolution: keep the incoming version (the file as it exists in the picked commit).
$ git status --short
DU feature.txt
?? part-a.log
?? part-b.log
?? part-b2.log
$ git add feature.txt
$ git cherry-pick --continue --no-edit
[main bb8becd] feature: the important fix we need on main
 Date: Thu Sep 3 19:54:14 2026 +0530
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 feature.txt

--- Verify the cherry-picked commit/change is now on main ---
$ git log --oneline main
bb8becd feature: the important fix we need on main
eb61eec main: change 3
d0c29c6 main: change 2
5180894 main: change 1
65f33e0 add line2 (with -a)
ab1a34c initial commit
$ cat feature.txt
feature work A
feature work B
TARGET: this is the one commit we will cherry-pick

CONCLUSION: main now has the one specific commit's change from feature-branch
(feature.txt with the fix), WITHOUT the other feature-branch-only commits
that main doesn't need.
